WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.552
- The process though,
you came back to that.

00:00:01.552 --> 00:00:02.640
- Exactly.
- Yeah.

00:00:02.640 --> 00:00:04.297
- Well, actually, that's
actually what drew me

00:00:04.297 --> 00:00:06.210
to asking him.

00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.280
- Yeah.

00:00:07.280 --> 00:00:09.007
- Because you, again, the
the longer you do this,

00:00:09.007 --> 00:00:13.440
the more you realize how integral

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:17.640
those people are to making
it all happen, you know?

00:00:17.640 --> 00:00:19.860
- My integral part is standing over there

00:00:19.860 --> 00:00:22.080
and he's been with me since
American Idol for 20 years.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:23.545
I've never done a tour without Jason.

00:00:23.545 --> 00:00:25.597
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:00:25.597 --> 00:00:27.480
Everybody, everybody, literally every.

00:00:27.480 --> 00:00:29.400
and he produces, we write together.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.800
Like, we're, like, the
best musical duo ever.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.633
I love us.

00:00:32.633 --> 00:00:34.110
But because we are different

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:35.250
and I think that's what's awesome.

00:00:35.250 --> 00:00:36.690
We bring something different to the table.

00:00:36.690 --> 00:00:39.930
And to have that stability
with someone in your career,

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:42.420
from that long ago,
and that you still gel,

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:45.420
and you still create with, is so...

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:46.470
it's rare.
- It's everything.

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:48.150
- It's rare and it's also everything.

00:00:48.150 --> 00:00:50.550
Like, I don't know a lot of
people that have that, you know,

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:52.620
and I, literally, was just
telling somebody the other,

00:00:52.620 --> 00:00:53.850
I was, like, I'm the luckiest person ever.

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:56.370
Like, people, like, my
career is also because of

00:00:56.370 --> 00:00:57.480
that man standing over there.

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.060
Like, they help you
create, they bring out you,

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.790
they make you comfortable,
'cause you know them well enough.

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:04.710
Like, it's just the best
collaborative process.

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:05.543
I agree with that.

00:01:05.543 --> 00:01:06.810
- Yeah, I'll agree with that.

00:01:06.810 --> 00:01:09.210
But your career is because
of you, essentially,

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:10.043
is because of you-

00:01:10.043 --> 00:01:11.629
- I just mean I have a
little bit to with it.

00:01:11.629 --> 00:01:12.780
- [Seal] You and your talent, you know.

00:01:12.780 --> 00:01:13.613
- I'm a little bit to do.

00:01:13.613 --> 00:01:15.420
That's what he would say.

00:01:15.420 --> 00:01:16.770
But no, I just mean, like,

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:18.630
but I do think that, you know,

00:01:18.630 --> 00:01:20.520
starting out, even like
starting at how I did,

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:21.720
like, these other, you know,

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:23.010
artists and contestants on these shows,

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:25.530
it's, like, I love so
many different sounds.

00:01:25.530 --> 00:01:28.170
So, to, kind of, drive home,
like, what I'm gonna focus on,

00:01:28.170 --> 00:01:29.003
it's hard.

00:01:29.003 --> 00:01:31.200
I'm ADHD, so he's been the
person to, kind of, be, like,

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.760
let's focus.

00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:33.593
- I gotta ask you,

00:01:33.593 --> 00:01:38.593
'cause I could never have
done what you what you did,

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:39.630
you know, in order to get to-

00:01:39.630 --> 00:01:42.060
- I love competition.
(audience laughs)

00:01:42.060 --> 00:01:45.060
- See, yeah, me too, me too,

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:45.893
but I just think it takes-

00:01:45.893 --> 00:01:47.109
- Even with yourself,
competing with yourself.

00:01:47.109 --> 00:01:50.550
- Yeah, but I just think
it takes a certain level

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:55.170
of courage and confidence
to be able to go on a show.

00:01:55.170 --> 00:01:56.003
- Yeah.

00:01:56.003 --> 00:01:57.030
- And break through that way.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:00.930
I mean, I'm not, you know,
being modest or anything.

00:02:00.930 --> 00:02:02.490
I could never have done that.

00:02:02.490 --> 00:02:03.730
I know what I'm capable of when I-

00:02:03.730 --> 00:02:04.950
- Which is hysterical, though,

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:07.680
because your voice is, like,
what people are looking for.

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:08.640
- I wouldn't have done it.

00:02:08.640 --> 00:02:10.200
I wouldn't have.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:13.200
It takes, I think, a
certain amount of courage

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.610
to put yourself out there.

00:02:15.610 --> 00:02:16.443
- Yeah.

00:02:16.443 --> 00:02:18.810
- And be judged in amongst
other people, right?

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:22.290
And be critiqued on a
show, on a world stage.

00:02:22.290 --> 00:02:27.290
I don't know if anyone realizes
how hard that is, you know,

00:02:27.540 --> 00:02:29.670
to actually put yourself out there,

00:02:29.670 --> 00:02:32.790
and people tell you how good
you were or how bad you were,

00:02:32.790 --> 00:02:36.450
and you having to take it, you
know, on a show like you did.

00:02:36.450 --> 00:02:39.510
I wouldn't have had
the courage to do that.

00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:41.670
And so, I have so much admiration.

00:02:41.670 --> 00:02:42.616
- Well, thank you.

00:02:42.616 --> 00:02:43.794
I think, though-
- But what was it like?

00:02:43.794 --> 00:02:44.627
- It was like really
good bootcamp, though,

00:02:44.627 --> 00:02:46.830
because it was really hard and
it was more hard, not for me,

00:02:46.830 --> 00:02:47.663
but to watch other people.

00:02:47.663 --> 00:02:48.930
I'm always that person, like,

00:02:48.930 --> 00:02:51.270
it's hard for me to watch other
people go through something

00:02:51.270 --> 00:02:53.670
and, like, other artists
were not handling it well,

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.140
like, what people would say online.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:57.600
And it was the first time
the show was on, or whatever.

00:02:57.600 --> 00:03:00.480
So, that was harder,
watching people, you know,

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.520
break their spirit a bit.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:03.353
- Yeah.
- I think.

00:03:03.353 --> 00:03:04.350
And that sucks.

00:03:04.350 --> 00:03:06.360
But I will say, it was a great bootcamp,

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.970
because after that I felt like,

00:03:08.970 --> 00:03:10.170
I mean, this industry is hard.

00:03:10.170 --> 00:03:11.250
You say you couldn't handle it,

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.620
but you did, because this
industry is not easy.

00:03:13.620 --> 00:03:16.050
Even if you're selling 8 million
albums, or doing whatever,

00:03:16.050 --> 00:03:18.150
there's always people just
trying to knock you down

00:03:18.150 --> 00:03:20.970
or say something just super (beeps)

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:22.415
I can't say that on TV, but-

00:03:22.415 --> 00:03:23.248
(audience laughs)

00:03:23.248 --> 00:03:25.397
- But you went from nothing

00:03:25.397 --> 00:03:26.670
to all of a sudden being exposed.

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:27.570
- But that's the trick, though.

00:03:27.570 --> 00:03:29.880
That's why I think that is the key.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.850
When you have no home,
my place had burned down,

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.700
I was living in my car for a bit,

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.963
like, I had nothing, I had nothing.

00:03:36.963 --> 00:03:39.360
And, I think, when you have nothing,

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:40.560
you have nothing to lose.

00:03:40.560 --> 00:03:42.990
So, you just show up and
you go, sure, you can laugh.

00:03:42.990 --> 00:03:44.550
But if I'm getting paid,

00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:46.170
I'm laughing all the way to the bank,

00:03:46.170 --> 00:03:47.783
so I'm, like... (laughs)

00:03:47.783 --> 00:03:48.616
(Seal laughs and applauds)
(audience applauds and cheers)

00:03:48.616 --> 00:03:49.449
Like, I think you don't...

00:03:49.449 --> 00:03:50.640
At that point, like, in my mind,

00:03:50.640 --> 00:03:53.490
literally, I didn't think
that it would go anywhere.

00:03:53.490 --> 00:03:55.230
I mean, a lot of people don't
go anywhere on those shows.

00:03:55.230 --> 00:03:56.063
You know what I'm saying?

00:03:56.063 --> 00:03:56.896
You don't know.

00:03:56.896 --> 00:03:58.020
And so I was, literally, just, like,

00:03:58.020 --> 00:03:59.460
I need to pay my water bill.

00:03:59.460 --> 00:04:00.660
I need to get housing.

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:04.920
I think when you're that
desperate, you don't...

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:07.980
All of that stuff is, like, I
don't even have time for that.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:09.930
Like, these are real issues I have.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:11.490
I think, when that is your...

00:04:11.490 --> 00:04:13.110
That's why I think when everybody's,

00:04:13.110 --> 00:04:14.407
like, they ask celebrities, like,

00:04:14.407 --> 00:04:15.930
"Oh, do you want your
kid in the business?"

00:04:15.930 --> 00:04:17.377
Which, I'm gonna ask, like,

00:04:17.377 --> 00:04:18.990
"Would you really want your kid

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:19.890
to thrive in this kinda business?"

00:04:19.890 --> 00:04:20.880
Because it's a hard one.

00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:24.925
Sometimes I think my kids
will never know what it's like

00:04:24.925 --> 00:04:28.110
to go without, to really
have that desperation,

00:04:28.110 --> 00:04:30.150
of, like, having to push
yourself, and go for it.

00:04:30.150 --> 00:04:32.077
And that's hard like to teach, you know.

00:04:32.077 --> 00:04:33.736
I don't know if you can teach that.

00:04:33.736 --> 00:04:34.569
- [Seal] It is hard.

00:04:34.569 --> 00:04:35.760
So, then you don't want
them to swallow your kids up

00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.920
in an industry that's hard.

00:04:37.920 --> 00:04:39.720
I don't know, what are your thoughts?

00:04:39.720 --> 00:04:41.825
Am I just dark, what?
(audience laughs)

00:04:41.825 --> 00:04:43.383
- No, not at all.

00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:45.870
'Cause I've often thought of that.

00:04:45.870 --> 00:04:49.620
My son, Henry, he sings
and he has a great voice.

00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:50.453
- Yeah.

00:04:50.453 --> 00:04:51.286
- He doesn't think so

00:04:51.286 --> 00:04:52.980
but he has a really great
husky voice, you know.

00:04:52.980 --> 00:04:54.920
- But his dad is you, that's hard.

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:55.753
(audience laughs)

00:04:55.753 --> 00:04:56.730
I'm just gonna say it.

00:04:56.730 --> 00:05:01.310
- But then, you know, if
that's what he wanted to do.

00:05:01.310 --> 00:05:02.442
- [Kelly] do it.

00:05:02.442 --> 00:05:07.080
- It's my job to just support him

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:09.000
and as much as-
- Yeah.

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:11.310
- As much as I can.

00:05:11.310 --> 00:05:13.410
I don't know, it's a tough one

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.410
because, obviously, you know,
we've traveled that road

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:19.290
and we know how difficult it can be.

00:05:19.290 --> 00:05:23.730
But, ultimately, my advice
to them is just be happy.

00:05:23.730 --> 00:05:24.563
- Yeah.

00:05:26.039 --> 00:05:27.450
- Do whatever, I don't care if it's, like,

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:30.570
if you've gotta go and like
sweep the streets, you know,

00:05:30.570 --> 00:05:31.743
or if you-

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.450
- Get one life, be happy
with what you're doing.

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:36.090
- Yeah, and just be happy.

00:05:36.090 --> 00:05:39.810
'Cause I really believe
that is the point of it all.

00:05:39.810 --> 00:05:40.643
- Yeah.

00:05:40.643 --> 00:05:44.370
- Is to try and figure out how
to be as happy as possible.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:46.590
Now, that sounds like a kind of, almost,

00:05:46.590 --> 00:05:48.540
flippant thing to say and as-

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:50.073
- No, it's simple, but it's hard.

00:05:50.073 --> 00:05:51.410
- It's really hard.
- Yeah.

00:05:51.410 --> 00:05:53.760
- If you think about it, because...

00:05:53.760 --> 00:05:56.970
Be happy and all that that entails.

00:05:56.970 --> 00:06:00.060
Can I be happy if this person isn't happy

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:02.111
or if that person's suffering, you know.

00:06:02.111 --> 00:06:03.020
- Yeah, or what society tells you,

00:06:03.020 --> 00:06:04.620
you should be happy if you're not yet.

00:06:04.620 --> 00:06:07.200
- Exactly, so if they, you know,

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:09.848
whatever they choose to
do, whether it's music,

00:06:09.848 --> 00:06:12.270
whether it's...

00:06:12.270 --> 00:06:14.820
My eldest daughter, Leni,

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:16.200
who was actually gonna be here today,

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:18.665
but she has to go back to New York.

00:06:18.665 --> 00:06:22.140
She's modeling, and I know
that's a kind of, you know,

00:06:22.140 --> 00:06:22.973
that's a...

00:06:24.326 --> 00:06:25.590
- A hard game as well, yeah.

00:06:25.590 --> 00:06:27.000
- Yeah, lots of rejection.

00:06:27.000 --> 00:06:28.596
A hard road to...

00:06:28.596 --> 00:06:31.680
And, you know, she has
a well-known mother.

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:32.677
- Never heard of her.

00:06:32.677 --> 00:06:34.985
(Kelly and audience laughing)

00:06:34.985 --> 00:06:38.160
- But, as long as she's happy.

00:06:38.160 --> 00:06:41.940
And, you know, and I will
say this, for the kids,

00:06:41.940 --> 00:06:43.470
I can't call them kids anymore,

00:06:43.470 --> 00:06:46.200
'cause they're teenagers,
they're young adults,

00:06:46.200 --> 00:06:50.430
but for my sons and
daughters, I will say this,

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:52.350
they got it a lot more figured out

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:55.740
than I ever did at their age, you know.

00:06:55.740 --> 00:06:56.573
- You've done a good job.

00:06:56.573 --> 00:07:00.810
- I find that I spend way too
much time worrying about them

00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:02.370
and, you know, if they'll find their way.

00:07:02.370 --> 00:07:04.620
But the way that they see the world

00:07:04.620 --> 00:07:06.090
is very different from the way

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:08.730
that we, as adults, see
the world, you know.

00:07:08.730 --> 00:07:12.570
Where we see problems, they
see solutions and vice versa.

00:07:12.570 --> 00:07:16.393
- Oh, I hope the younger
generation figures it out. (laughs)

